      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{Localization relying on wireless ultra-wideband (UWB) signaling is investigated. Various localization alternatives are considered and the UWB time-of-arrival based one is found to have highest ranging accuracy. The challenges in UWB positioning problems, such as multiple-access interference, multipath and non-line-of-sight propagation are presented along with the fundamental limits for time-of-arrival estimation and time-of-arrival-based positioning. To reduce complexity of optimal schemes achieving those limits, suboptimal alternatives are also developed and analyzed. Moreover, a hybrid scheme that incorporates time-of-arrival and signal strength measurements is investigated.}
      \field{title}{Localization via {Ultra}-{Wideband} {Radios}}
